    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96773" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῐβ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>walker, traveller</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιδεύς</span> cod.); cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στειβεύς</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fuller</i>, who cleans clothes by treading them, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				3p.173
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1087.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.30
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				376
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>one who tracks out</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. κύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					1.463
				</span></i>
			.</div>
